    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "## Owner decision recorded: Option A ACCEPTED (narrow scope)\n\nThe owner explicitly chose **Option A, curated two-person bearer capabilities**, for the initial owner + one trusted invitee pilot: two distinct battle/side-scoped tokens and no passkey/account service for this pilot. Owner accepts the specifically documented bearer-theft limitation: an active stolen bearer is indistinguishable from its intended holder until revoked.\n\n**Scope:** This settles **only the Option A vs B auth-model choice**, a part of PA-02. It **does not** accept browser localStorage/IndexedDB persistence risk, exact origin/CSP, invite-delivery and device-recovery procedure, PA-03..09 operator/key custody/retention/backup, safe generation readback, staging/deployment, real-player invitation or merging the PR. Those stay owner-gated.\n\n**Verified current Draft PR #450:** HEAD `a76ff571529733b237173424c30972a594869982`, one documentation file, 5 ahead/0 behind exact base main@31b7a077820914e92de81239e5ab4099e3dfa558. All **8/8 exact-head CI checks SUCCESS**. The previously found lost-replace-response gap is correctly described in current spec as **BLOCKED / STOP** until independently verified read-only operator generation inspection is available; no guessed SQL/readback or blind retry is allowed.\n\n**Codex routing:** If updating this PR's written decision table/status, use the **SAME Codex thread for PR #450**, and keep all other PA statuses open. Next `CHAT03-TWO-PERSON-REMOTE-CLIENT-TRANSPORT` is a **NEW Codex thread/branch** only when storage/exact client origin+CSP/recovery policies are approved. Absolutely no Cloudflare, D1, invite or main writes from the present owner auth choice.\n\nNotion memory recorded with top `MEMORY_REV: 2026-10-28-CHAT03-OWNER-APPROVES-OPTION-A-PR450-R206`.",
